### Career Stats Service - HTTP tests
# Instructions: Start the service (default port 5004) and run these requests with the VSCode REST Client or curl.

### Health check
GET http://localhost:5004/health
Accept: application/json

# Expected: 200, JSON { "status": "ok" }

### List all careers (payscale data)
GET http://localhost:5004/api/careers
Accept: application/json

# Expected: 200, JSON { success: true, count: <number>, careers: [ ... ] }

### Search careers by query (case-insensitive)
GET http://localhost:5004/api/careers/search?q=developer
Accept: application/json

# Expected: 200, JSON { success: true, count: <number>, careers: [ ...matching jobs... ] }

### Search with empty query (should return full list)
GET http://localhost:5004/api/careers/search
Accept: application/json

# Expected: 200, same as /api/careers

### Get aggregated salary stats
GET http://localhost:5004/api/careers/stats
Accept: application/json

# Expected: 200, JSON { success: true, stats: { total_jobs, min_salary, max_salary, avg_salary, median_salary } }

### Non-existing route (verify 404 or default behavior)
GET http://localhost:5004/api/unknown
Accept: application/json

# Expected: 404 or other appropriate status
